.TH FL-KEYRING 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop 0.1.4" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
fl-keyring \- passwords and keys
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfl-keyring\fR [\fB\-\-page\fR passwords|ssh|gpg]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBPasswords\fR lists the passwords programs keep in the Secret Service
(GNOME Keyring, KeePassXC, KWallet): web sites, Wi-Fi networks, mail
accounts, SSH key passphrases. A keyring is unlocked with its own password
when needed; passwords can be shown, copied (and taken off the clipboard
again after 30 seconds), changed, renamed, added and deleted, and new
keyrings made.
.PP
\fBSSH Keys\fR lists the keys in \fI~/.ssh\fR with their fingerprints:
generate an Ed25519 key, copy a public key, change a passphrase, delete a
key. \fBGPG Keys\fR lists your GnuPG keys: generate one, import, copy a
public key, delete.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBssh-keygen\fR(1), \fBgpg\fR(1), \fBsecret-tool\fR(1)
